# P&L Variance Summary – FY2025

## Year-over-Year Performance (vs. Same Period Last Year)

**Overall picture: Severe deterioration.** The business swung from profit to loss.

| Line Item | Movement | Magnitude | Assessment |
|-----------|----------|-----------|------------|
| **Operating Profit** | Profit → Loss | RM –4.68M (–371%) | **SEVERE** |
| **Net Profit** | Profit → Loss | RM –3.34M (–242%) | **SEVERE** |
| **Gross Profit** | Decline | RM –2.19M (–28%) | Material unfavourable |
| **Operating Costs** | Spike | RM +2.49M (+38%) | Material unfavourable |
| **Cost of Sales** | Rise | RM +3.82M (+5.3%) | Moderate unfavourable |
| **Net Sales** | Growth | RM +1.63M (+2%) | On track |
| **Other Income** | Surge | RM +1.34M (+1,134%) | Favourable |

**Margin erosion:**
- Gross Margin fell 2.9pp (9.8% → 6.9%)
- Net Margin fell 4.1pp (1.7% → –2.4%)

**Key drivers:** Despite 2% sales growth, COGS and OpEx surged faster than revenue, compressing margins and flipping profitability negative. Other income (+RM 1.46M) partially offset losses.

---

## Budget Variance (vs. Approved Budget)

**Status: Essentially on track.** All line items are within ±0.0% of budget — variances are immaterial (RM –4 to RM 1).

- Net Sales, COGS, Gross Profit, Operating Costs, and Net Profit all hit budget targets.
- The loss (RM –1.96M) was **budgeted**.

---

## Bottom Line

- **YoY:** Business is performing significantly worse. Profitability collapsed due to cost overruns despite modest revenue growth.
- **Budget:** Execution is precise; the negative result was expected and approved.
- **Action required:** The budget itself was built on loss assumptions. Investigate root causes of the 38% OpEx increase and 5.3% COGS increase relative to last year.

